otengine/godot/pull/105554#issuecomment-2816820489","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105554","id":2816820489,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n5UUJ","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T18:40:57Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T18:53:46Z","body":"I understand if you don't think this feature is worth adding to the engine, but since the change was made to EditorHelp, the icons are supported in the local docs (in the script tab), tooltips, and it also works for user-written documentation (through the `##` comments), the only thing as far as I'm aware that is not supported is the website docs (they use a separate system through `.rst` files).\r\n\r\nBelow, I modified the TileMap.xml file to display the button's icon next to where it is referenced. This reduces ambiguity and helps the user find UI elements easier because they have a reference for what it looks like.\r\n<img width=\"650\" alt=\"Documentation with icon\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/182c7fea-438c-4412-9146-5e79506d2745\" />\r\n\r\n","author_associati